<title>USA: Entergy Ark. nuke returns to full power.</title>
<headline>Entergy Ark. nuke returns to full power.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Entergy Corp's 836 megawatt (MW) Arkansas nuclear unit 1, which restarted late Thursday after a Sept 12 maintenance and refueling outage, returned to full power this weekend, the company said Monday.</p>
<p>The Russellville, Ark., unit was originally expected to restart Oct 20, but it was delayed following an insulation fire on Oct 17.</p>
<p>The adjacent unit, with a generating capacity of 858 MW, is also operating at full power.</p>
<p>--H McCulloch, New York Power Desk +212-859-1628</p>
